#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260013 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20b289d4-96a7-5d1b-9714-6afabab4804d" :knowledge-point/title "Further Determining Rates of Change in Geometrical Settings"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "217b3cdf-d9a6-5d92-af20-1a2fc17eaac9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260015}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "217b3cdf-d9a6-5d92-af20-1a2fc17eaac9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260015} :answer-field/id #uuid "9addb752-1c9d-5aa6-8cbb-442afe3f39ef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260014}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0a48171a-86f8-5d26-b8a7-cb6fe266dbbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-343499" :question/problem "The surface area $A$ of a cube is increasing. Find the instantaneous rate at which the surface area of the cube is changing with respect to its side length at the moment when the side length of the cube is equal to $3\\,\\text{in}.$\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at the moment when its side length is $3$ inches is equal to\n{{field-1}} ${\\text{in}}^{2}/\\text{in}.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that the surface area of a cube with side length $s$ is given by \n\n$$\nA=A(s)=6{s}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTaking the derivative, the rate of change of $A(s)$ with respect to $s$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{'}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(6{s}^{2}) \\\\  & =6(2s) \\\\  & =12s,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand evaluating at $s=3$ gives\n\n$$\n{A}^{'}(3)=12(3)=36.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate at which the surface area of the cube is changing when its side length is $3\\,\\text{in}$, is $36$ ${\\text{in}}^{2}/\\text{in}.$"}]}
